II (1 mark for organ, 1 mark for function).

Three from:

• mouth: chews/ breaks down food into smaller

pieces / produces saliva;

• oesophagus (gullet): move food from mouth to

stomach;

•

stomach: produces digestive enzymes;

• pancreas: produces digestive enzymes;

• liver: makes bile;

• ileum (small intestine) produces digestive

enzymes I absorbs products of digestion;

• colon (large intestine): absorbs excess water;

• rectum: stores waste (faeces).

Iii (1 mark for system, 2 marks for organs).

Two from:

• breathing system: trachea, lung, diaphragm;

• circulatory system: artery, vein, heart;

• musculoskeletal system: muscle, joint, (named)

bone;

• nervous system: brain, spinal cord;

• reproductive system: testis, ovary, uterus, penis;

• excretory system: kidney, bladder.

